cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "tg-ai: a local Telegram MCP server for AI agents"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: anrysys
    website: "https://github.com/anrysys"
repository-code: "https://github.com/anrysys/tg-ai"
url: "https://anrysys.github.io/tg-ai/"
abstract: >-
  tg-ai is a local Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that gives an AI agent
  controlled access to a person's own Telegram account over MTProto. It can send
  messages as the account owner, read replies live, run full-text search across a
  local PostgreSQL archive of the account's private chat history, and supply a
  per-conversation writing-style profile (the Dialog Persona) so drafted replies
  match how the owner actually writes to each individual correspondent. Anti-ban
  guardrails, including a non-overridable refusal to message strangers, are part
  of the design rather than a configuration option.
keywords:
  - model-context-protocol
  - mcp-server
  - telegram
  - mtproto
  - ai-agents
  - llm-tools
  - full-text-search
  - postgresql
  - local-first
  - writing-style
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-09-11"
